# Evidence of Life agent rules

You are working in **evidenceoflife-v2**: Vite 5 + React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind 3 + Supabase.

## Always

- Read `llms.txt` / `AGENTS.md` for map and policy.
- Run `npm run typecheck` after TS changes (SWC does not type-check builds).
- Run `npm test` after logic changes.
- Do not fabricate features, APIs, metrics, or green CI.
- Never commit secrets; use `.env.example` only as the template.
- Keep diffs small; one concern per change.
- Prefer existing HSL design tokens; dark mode is primary.
- Verify UI on `http://localhost:8080/demo-app` before claiming visual success.

## Separate review required

Treat these as security-sensitive — do not mix into unrelated feature PRs:

- `supabase/migrations/**`
- Auth (`useAuth`, Auth pages)
- Edge auth / OAuth (`supabase/functions/_shared/**`, `google-calendar-*`)
- Storage privacy (`momentPhotos`, `StorageImage`, photo bucket policies)

## Do not

- Invent integrations that are not in the repo
- Weaken JWT / HMAC OAuth / private photo signed-URL model without explicit task + tests
- Refactor large view files when a local fix suffices
- Add markdown docs unless asked (except when the task is documentation)
